      "text": "**The north has better air** in the latest readings I could verify, from **12:00 pm Singapore time on October 17**: 1‑hour PM2.5 was **91 µg/m³ in the north**, versus **206 µg/m³ in the west**. The 24‑hour PSI was also lower in the north (**136 vs. 178**). ([checkpointsg.com](https://www.checkpointsg.com/haze))\n\nThe west’s immediate PM2.5 reading was in NEA’s **High** band, while the north’s was **Elevated**—but both readings may have changed since that update. ([haze.gov.sg](https://www.haze.gov.sg/))",
